yupiter
-------

yupiter is a freestanding C library for Linux on aarch64 and x86_64.
It provides its own entry point, system-call layer, formatted output
and allocator, and links without a C library or C++ runtime.

The public interface is ISO C17 and usable from C and C++.  The
implementation is ISO C++23, built freestanding.  Other operating
systems and architectures are rejected at configure time.

Status: stable.  Current release 1.0.2; SOVERSION 1.  Exported symbols,
signatures, C linkage and public structure layouts are stable within
the 1.x series.


Build
-----

    ./configure
    make
    make check
    make install

Builds libyupiter.a and libyupiter.so by default.  Run
./configure --help for prefix, build type, heap size and library
selection.  See docs/building.


Documentation
------------

docs/README lists every document and the reading order.


